    <item>
      <title>L&amp;T and BAE Begin BvS10 Sindhu Production for High-Altitude Warfare</title>
      <link>https://neodymium.world/articles/l-t-and-bae-begin-bvs10-sindhu-production-for-high-altitude-warfare-215345.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://neodymium.world/articles/l-t-and-bae-begin-bvs10-sindhu-production-for-high-altitude-warfare-215345.html</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Amarjeet Singh</dc:creator>
      <!-- Description: executive summary or first key takeaway only (no full HTML body).
           This keeps the RSS file small and avoids duplicate-content issues with Google. -->
      <description><![CDATA[
        L&amp;T and BAE Systems have formally commenced production of the BvS10 Sindhu ATVs for the Indian Army, fundamentally altering high-altitude logistical sustainment across the Ladakh sector and the Rann of Kutch.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The platform features a unique two-cabin articulated design optimized for extreme snow, vertical gradients, and treacherous marshlands.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Deployment spans the high-altitude Ladakh sector along the LAC and the salt flats of the Rann of Kutch, enhancing year-round logistical sustainment.
        [SPLIT]
        🔗 Read full report → https://neodymium.world/articles/l-t-and-bae-begin-bvs10-sindhu-production-for-high-altitude-warfare-215345.html
      ]]></description>
      
